Negative control for the mm_list use-after-free fix: revert the list_del.

b38e70bc1 ("skas: take the mm back out of mm_list when starting its stub
fails") added the list_del below, and recorded that it had no reproducing
control because start_userspace() cannot be made to fail on demand. The
injection patch (config/inject-stub-fail.patch) supplies that failure, and this
patch removes the fix, so the two kernels differ only in the piece under test.

With a stub failure injected, init_new_context() jumps to out_free with the mm
still on mm_list. The caller's failure path does not call destroy_context(), so
the mm is freed while linked. The next mm allocation reuses that slab object
and list_add()s it again, which folds mm_list into a self-referential cycle;
the next walk -- mm_sigchld_irq(), on any stub dying -- never terminates while
holding mm_list_lock, so the run hangs. The fixed kernel takes the mm back out
first and stays healthy.

The boot job requires this control to reach the expected verdict (a hang, not a
marker); a control that does not reproduce is a failure of the control, because
it would mean the guest never drove start_userspace() into the error path.

Apply with:  git apply tools/um-arm64/config/control-mm-list.patch
diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/skas/mmu.c b/arch/um/kernel/skas/mmu.c
index 2bf795439..2ef58ee9b 100644
--- a/arch/um/kernel/skas/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/skas/mmu.c
@@ -85,15 +85,6 @@ int init_new_context(struct task_struct *task, struct mm_struct *mm)
 	return 0;
 
  out_free:
-	/*
-	 * The mm is about to be freed by the caller, and mm_init()'s failure path
-	 * does not call destroy_context() -- so this list_del has no counterpart.
-	 * Without it mm_list keeps a pointer into freed memory and the next walk of
-	 * it, mm_sigchld_irq() on any stub dying, reads it: an ENOMEM while starting
-	 * a stub becomes a use-after-free somewhere else.
-	 */
-	scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &mm_list_lock)
-		list_del(&mm->context.list);
 	free_pages(new_id->stack, ilog2(STUB_DATA_PAGES));
  out:
 	return ret;
